Hello all,

I'm still moving steadily through the NetHack alphabet and here is the
news from Hayden4 (my 4th attempt) and his successful adventure.

I started out with the minetown protection run (as usual) and am
finding that if I can survive the run, the rest of the game is the
easier part.  I credit cloned and priced my loot in two general stores
to start.  Then I went to Sokoban and went as far as I could before
the mimcs stopped me.  Somehow my pet was killed in the mines and I
was faced with the decision to forget the run and level up or make a
break for the temple.   Since I had found a wand of digging I decided
to zap my way into Minetown and see if I could reach the temple before
being mobbed.  Well, it worked beautifully and with my 9 points of
intrinsic AC I was ready for action.   Whew!  That was actually the
hardest part of the game.  I donated quite a bit of gold throughout
the game thanks to having 5 temples and Ludios generated, and ended up
with an intrinsic AC = -5 all from donating to priests.  That helped
make up for the lack of ?oEA and magic markers.

I decided that in this game I was going to play with the Eye of the
Aethiopica and with an early magic lamp and a coaligned altar on level
2, I got my wish.  That was my only wish in the game and although
powerful, its biggest impact was in magic mapping Gehennom (45%
failure), casting create monster for cockatrice corpses, and
teleporting through the ascension run .  I didn't use the full effect
of the mana regeneration because I did not do any altar camping but I
did use it at the castle level to generate a cockatrice corpse for use
against the soldiers.  I probably could have saved myself a few
thousand turns if I had done a better job of stash management.

The other thing about this game was that I kept losing things, mainly
books.  I lost all 3 books that I started with and never did find my
spellbook of charm monster.  I know that I sold them in the early game
but I never saw them again and suspect that a gelatinous cube ate
them.

A few things that I was missing were:
ring of conflict -- I did okay without it, but on the Plane of Air I
saw a lot more action and had to teleport away a lot more Air
Elementals.
ring of free action -- did not need very often although not having it
made melee'ing gelatinous cubes more dangerous and I did lose 100hp on
the Astral Plan while paralyzed.
magic markers -- never found one
?oEA -- very few of these and had +5, +5, +1, +0, +0, +0 armor
?oGD - only had two for the planes
T-shirt -- never found a t-shirt.

Throughout the game I was very much lacking in identify scrolls,
finding less than 12 and only having one yield a full inventory
identify and no spellbook of identify.  I did have a wand of
enlightenment and a sink that helped me identify rings and amulets.
Given the constraint I should have been more careful and there were a
few times where I could have identified the ring or amulet just by
trying it on uncursed, for example adornment and strangulation.  The
wand of enlightenment allowed me to identify teleport control which is
one of my favorites.  It was fun adapting to not having Identify and
although I could have wished for a spellbook I wanted to see if I
could limit myself to "just" the Eye.

Just before descending into Gehennom I was lucky and found a spellbook
of magic mapping.  That was fantastic and made the mazes painless.
Finding this book convinced me to not wish for a spellbook of
identify.  If I hadn't found one or the other then I probably would
nto had the patience and would have used a wish.  I did not do much of
any loot collecting in Gehennom, by then I was ready to find the VS
and ascend.  The only thing I did consistently was hunt minotaurs
because I was short on wands of digging.

In addition to identify scrolls I was also short on enchant armor
scrolls and never found a magic marker.  I only had the wand of death
from Orcus and after using it only once against Rodney on the plane of
earth, it was exploded by an eel on the plane of water.  I was doing
some inventory management next to the portal on the plane of water
when somehow I got in the wrong bubble and had to levitate back to the
portal.  An electic eel zapped me and I lost my wand of death and a
wand of teleport.  I think the odds of that are pretty small because I
thought that MC=3 protects against shock attacks.

For conducts I held to poly*less and genoless.  Liches were an
annoyance but never too big of a threat.  (M)MF were scared off by
Elbereth and/or killed with darts.

I came prepared for the Cyclops with a wand of sleep and slaying him
in his sleep was easy.  I blessed the staff and wielded it for the
rest of the game, except of course when a cockatrice corpse was
handy.

I cursed teleport scrolled my way from the Wizards first level to his
cell and then back down to the VS.  Rodney was killed with a
cockatrice corpse.  I used 2 scrolls getting to the left side of the
sanctum.  I made it into the temple and killed the priest but Yeenoghu
grabbed the amulet from the ground and teleported to the upstairs.
So, I eyeported out and then went back down the stairs.  Once I had
the upstairs blocked I meleed the Demon and grabbed the Amulet.

For the ascension run I started with 20 scrolls of teleport, 160
power, 6 cursed potions of gain level, and maybe 35 teleport zaps.
Here is where the Eye really shined, I used intrinsic teleportitis to
zoom me through the levels and when low on pw, I read scrolls and
zapped my wands at myself.   I used jumping boots with Haste Self to
zip across the no teleport levels.  I never saw the Wizard until the
plane of earth.  With the eye I could ^T so frequently that I was able
to save zaps for the endgame.  At the start of the plane of earth I
had 20 zaps left in my wands; I used 7 zaps on Air and 1 potion of
full healing, 0 zaps on earth, water and fire, and 5 zaps on the
Astral Plane.  I tried to use my wand of slow monster on the plane of
air but the elementals kept re-engulfing me and I had to teleport them
away while engulfed.

To find the portals I used a crystal ball on the plane of earth while
in the starting chamber, monster observation on the plane of air, the
crystal ball on the plane of fire while engulfed by a fire vortex, and
2 scrolls of GD on the plane of water.  No problem.

I found the altar on the second try.  The only challenge were two
purple lichs but with sufficient melee they were both taken care of.
I meleed Death twice (no problem) and dodged pestilence.  I was not
looking forward to fighting Famine because I had very little food and
I did not know what to expect.

I tried to move fast in this game but only managed to get into the 50k
turn range. Sorry this post is so choppy but it's late and at least
it's something.  Hopefully someone can take something useful from
it.

